   },
   "notes": "Second-order Murnaghan means quadratic K(P), not BM2. Static P0 offset plus zero-point and absolute Debye terms. V0/K0 are adopted low-temperature constraints, not room-temperature zero-pressure solid values. Eq. (1) has an apparent extra equals sign before PT; additive form follows the described decomposition and Eqs. (2)-(6). Printed P_z0 does not exactly cancel Eq. (2) at V0 with printed gamma1/theta0; retain all source values. Other-temperature isotherms in Fig.2 are predictions, not measured points. No solid-solid transition observed through 8.17 GPa. Uncertainty confidence level and covariance unspecified."
  }
